      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "High poly avatars are already prevented by the VRC SDK, and yes I know about the people that understand C# and are able to disable this protocol, and the avatar lock zone should be an optional thing for maps to were instead of displaying a visible barrier preventing the player to move past, should instead just disable all triggers that start the game *Client side/local* preventing the player from joining in.\n\nBut you would have to also think about, how can this feature be bypassed, and how can this feature also be used against other players that are obeying the avatar lock zone with hacked/modded clients?\n\nIn my opinion, This is an interesting feature, but I would rather just stick with people that I know and trust on vrchat and go to a friends+/friends/invite+/invite room and make sure everyone knows the rules before starting, so one, you can build trust with your friends that they won't cheat and everyone can have a little more fun, and two, allow for someone that has a more interesting avatar for the mini-game can use theirs instead of a \"cheaper\" avatar.\n\n\nAnd besides, if people do use broken, laggy, or tiny avatars, just block the avatar to show the grey neutral avatar, and their hitbox/pill will go back to standard size.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
