  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Avatar lock zone prevents people using broken, large, small, high poly, loud avatars to disrupt/troll/lagg or in some cases cause distress to fellow players in the mini-games\n\nThe avatar lock zone will prevent anyone not using the Id of a model provided by the World entering a stage or a match this will give a huge quality of life to mini-games and even encourage more creativity for mini-games. lets say one guy needs to play a monster so this player needs to choose the monster avatar that has been provided by the world to play the game.\n\n\nwhen you are using avatar that is not provided by the game a barrier will prevent you to gain access, when entering a avatar lock zone with the correct avatar the avatar menu will be fully locked in till leaving the area then you can regain access.\n\nI believe a system should also be allowed if a world creator wants to set it up so only the public avatars may enter the restricted avatar zone as well.\n\nThe avatar lock Zone will also greatly improve life on large scale events to reduce lagg or interference.\n\nThis idea became about when a player would bring a invisible or broken and even ant sized avatar to the wild west shooting game preventing them to take damage.\n\nThanks for reading I hope you like this idea as well.\n\nAlso this may encourage prop hunt maps im just saying.\n\nand to build on this system I would say if it was possible you may be this tall or this short to enter for any avatar or even this maybe the system will prevent a user with high polys to enter the match/room.\nalso suggest the barrier could be turned off by the world owner if she/he chooses.\n",
